  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You will be given two arrays AAA and BBB, each of length NNN. For some value KKK, let's call an array CCC `good` if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n\n0≤Ci≤Bi0\\le C_i \\le B_i0≤Ci​≤Bi​ for (1≤i≤N)(1 \\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N)\n**At least** KKK elements in the array must be equal to 000.\n∑i=1NAi=∑i=1NCi\\sum_{i=1}^N A_i = \\sum_{i=1}^N C_i ∑i=1N​Ai​=∑i=1N​Ci​\nAmong all the `good` arrays CCC, let result(K)result(K)result(K) denote the **minimum** value of ∑i=1N∣Ai−Ci∣\\sum_{i=1}^N |A_i-C_i|∑i=1N​∣Ai​−Ci​∣. If no good array is possible, result(K)=−1result(K) = -1result(K)=−1.\n\nFind the value result(K)result(K)result(K) for all (0≤K&lt;N)(0\\le K \\lt N)(0≤K&lt;N).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the array AAA.\nThe third line contains NNN integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​, the array BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN space-separated integers, result(K)result(K)result(K) for (0≤K&lt;N)(0 \\le K \\lt N)(0≤K&lt;N).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1001 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 1001≤Ai​,Bi​≤100",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 100100100."
    ],
